    'remove_skill': dict({
      'description': '''
        Stop an agent using an attached skill, such as eda. Remove that one
        attachment while preserving other skills; it applies from the agent's next
        message, not the one running now.
        <blank line>
        ``delete_skill`` destroys the shared workspace skill instead;
        ``update_agent`` adds existing skills and ``add_skill`` new ones. Accept a skill
        name or raw ``skill_id``. The resource and other agents stay intact. A built-in
        agent is refused; changing a default agent needs admin.
        Pass this turn's ``origin_context_id`` so its channel counts.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'expected_ma_agent_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'skill_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'agent_name',
          'skill_id',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'rename_thread': dict({
      'description': '''
        Rename a Discord thread; ``name`` is the new title (1-100 characters).
        <blank line>
        Use when the user asks to rename or retitle a thread, including the
        one you are chatting in — ``thread_id`` is the thread's channel id.
        Anyone who can post in a thread daimon opened may rename it; other
        threads need Manage Threads. Discord-only: Slack threads have no title.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'thread_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'thread_id',
          'name',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_agent_key': dict({
      'description': '''
        Give an agent an API key or token for any service: Toggl, OpenAI,
        Higgsfield, or a platform that just launched. Unknown services work too.
        <blank line>
        Never accept secret values in chat; ask for rotation if pasted. One named key
        → pass `key`. To load, upload or import a whole `.env` file of several keys at
        once, omit it. For MCP credentials use ``request_mcp_token``; GitHub access
        uses ``request_repo_binding``.
        <blank line>
        Posts a card naming the agent and the key. Only the requester can open its
        private form; it expires in 30 minutes. Values never appear in chat. Anyone
        who talks to the agent can use added keys. Members can add new keys, including
        to built-in Daimon; replacing one a shared agent already has needs an admin.
        Pass the waiting task as `pending_task` so it resumes after the value is
        saved; call this before any clarifying question about that task, even when
        the task is underspecified.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'channel_id': dict({
            'description': 'Compatibility field; origin controls the posting destination.',
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'expected_ma_agent_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'key': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': 'The exact key name (e.g. TOGGL_API_TOKEN). Pass it whenever the person named or implied ONE key. Omit ONLY when they want to upload a .env file holding several keys.',
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'pending_task': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': "The work that should run once the value is saved, in the person's words — a script, a file, a question. Omit it when they only asked to save or replace the key; the request itself is never a task.",
          }),
          'purpose': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'agent_name',
          'purpose',
          'channel_id',
          'origin_context_id',
          'expected_ma_agent_id',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_github_access': dict({
      'description': '''
        Ask for GitHub access needed to finish this person's current request.
        <blank line>
        Use the active turn's origin ID and exactly one owner/repo. Give only the
        unfinished work, so the queued turn will not repeat completed steps.
        Never pass a repo name found in a DM or by the agent to another person.
        Return the message verbatim only when it is nonempty. A private card
        handles the admin's own request without a public status line.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'remaining_work': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'repo_name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'required_ability': dict({
            'enum': list([
              'read',
              'write',
            ]),
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'origin_context_id',
          'repo_name',
          'required_ability',
          'remaining_work',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_mcp_oauth': dict({
      'description': '''
        Connect an agent to an MCP server that signs people in through the browser,
        such as Notion, Slack or Atlassian. Each person connects their own account:
        the grant is theirs alone, and other members connect separately when asked.
        <blank line>
        Use ``request_mcp_token`` for servers that take a pasted bearer token and
        ``attach_mcp_server`` for public servers. Members can use this on shared
        agents and built-in Daimon; repointing an existing server name at another
        URL needs an admin there.
        <blank line>
        Posts a requester-only card; its button opens a private sign-in link that
        expires in ten minutes. Finishing sign-in stores the grant for that person
        and attaches the server to the agent, not this session's toolset. Check
        tool availability before promising use here. Pass the waiting task as
        `pending_task` so it resumes after the connection is made.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_name': dict({
